"1885", "page_start": "1885", "journal_title": "Found.Phys."}}, "record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2979694"}}, {"reference": {"publication_info": {"journal_volume": "68", "artid": "063610", "journal_title": "Phys.Rev.A"}}, "record": {"$ref": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/2991057"}}, {"reference": {"publication_info": {"journal_volume": "55", "artid": "303", "page_start": "303", "journal_title": "EPL"}}}], "number_of_pages": 23, "referenced_authors_bais": ["C.G.Shull.1", "W.De.Baere.3", "S.Durr.3", "W.Treimer.1", "J.Petschinka.1", "R.Landauer.1", "M.G.M.Gramegna.1", "M.Golshani.12", "G.Rempe.1", "S.Goldstein.1", "T.Nonn.1", "L.H.Germer.1", "L.Hackermuller.2", "P.Ghose.1", "D.Bohm.1", "M.V.Vicari.1", "E.Joos.1", "S.Uttenthaler.2", "G.Brida.1", "M.Gramegna.1", "B.G.Englert.1", "W.Struyve.1", "H.D.Zeh.1", "B.Brezger.1", "D.M.Appleby.1", "R.Omnes.1", "A.Viale.1", "S.Guha.2", "S.Mancini.1", "M.Arndt.1", "E.Guay.1", "J.A.Barrett.1", "R.Gahler.1", "G.Falzetta.1", "O.Akhavan.2", "L.Marchildon.1", "W.Mampe.1", "C.Novero.1", "E.Predazzi.1", "J.Sau.5", "D.Durr.1", "A.S.Majumdar.1", "Nino.Zanghi.1", "R.Bonifacio.5", "M.Genovese.1", "A.Zeilinger.1", "E.Cagliero.1", "C.M.Davisson.1", "W.G.Unruh.1", "H.Nikolic.1"], "figures": [{"filename": "fig1.png", "material": "preprint", "caption": "(a) Comparison between experimental data ($\\circ$) and the intensity obtained from quantum trajectory ($\\bullet$) and SQM (full line) calculations for a double--slit experiment with cold neutrons \\cite{Zeilinger1}. (b) Sample of trajectories illustrating the dynamics of the results shown in part (a).", "label": "fig:1", "source": "arxiv", "key": "33b20571c141f3f1cb110f5e1c64baff", "url": "https://inspirehep.net/files/33b20571c141f3f1cb110f5e1c64baff"}, {"filename": "fig2.png", "material": "preprint", "caption": "Left: Intensity obtained from quantum trajectories ($\\bullet$) and SQM (full line) for: (a) total coherence ($\\tau_c = \\infty$) and (b) null coherence ($\\tau_c = 0$). Right: Samples of trajectories illustrating the dynamics of the results shown in the left part.", "label": "fig:2", "source": "arxiv", "key": "3320fabdf8ab2a8cd3cb2eb70874f872", "url": "https://inspirehep.net/files/3320fabdf8ab2a8cd3cb2eb70874f872"}, {"filename": "fig3.png", "material": "preprint", "caption": "Quantum trajectories for two different contexts: (a) slits independently open and (b) slits simultaneously open with $\\tau_c = 0$.", "label": "fig:3", "source": "arxiv", "key": "fcb970518c8177d03906b87a1951e964", "url": "https://inspirehep.net/files/fcb970518c8177d03906b87a1951e964"}], "legacy_version": "20190508165247.0", "inspire_categories": [{"term": "General Physics"}, {"term": "Quantum Physics", "source": "arxiv"}], "legacy_creation_date": "2006-02-15", "preprint_date": "2003-10", "author_count": 2, "public_notes": [{"source": "arXiv", "value": "8 pages, 3 figures"}], "first_author": {"full_name": "Sanz, A.S.", "last_name": "Sanz", "first_name": "A.S.", "recid": 1972197}, "control_number": 640163, "dois": [{"source": "ADS", "value": "10.1140/epjd/e2007-00191-8"}, {"material": "publication", "source": "arXiv", "value": "10.1140/epjd/e2007-00191-8"}], "earliest_date": "2003-10", "document_type": ["article"], "texkeys": ["Sanz:2003wy"], "abstracts": [{"value": "The effects of decoherence in interference phenomena are analyzed by defining a new class of quantum trajectories associated to the reduced density matrix of the system. In particular, this analysis is illustrated here by the double-slit experiment, a paradigm of quantum interference. As is well-known, in this experiment, the interference arises from the possibility for a particle to follow two different paths, from each slit to the detector. Within our trajectory description, based on Bohmian mechanics, we show that decoherence does not ensure that the particle motion related to one of those pathways is unaffected by the other one. Quantum mechanically decoherence suppresses the interference produced by the coherent superposition of the partial waves corresponding to each pathway. This gives rise to a classical-like intensity pattern, i.e. identical to that directly obtained from the sum of the intensities associated to those partial waves. However, the topology of the trajectories here defined reveals that the particle motion is strongly influenced by both pathways even in the case of full decoherence."}, {"source": "arXiv", "value": "A complete theoretical treatment in many problems relevant to physics, chemistry, and biology requires considering the action of the environment over the system of interest. Usually the environment involves a relatively large number of degrees of freedom, this making the problem numerically intractable from a purely quantum-mechanical point of view. To overcome this drawback, a new class of quantum trajectories is proposed. These trajectories, based on the same grounds as Bohmian ones, are solely associated to the system reduced density matrix, since the evolution of the environment degrees of freedom is not considered explicitly. Within this approach, environment effects come into play through a time-dependent damping factor that appears in the system equations of motion. Apart from their evident computational advantage, this type of trajectories also results very insightful to understand the system decoherence. In particular, here we show the usefulness of these trajectories analyzing decoherence effects in interference phenomena, taking as a working model the well-known double-slit experiment.", "abstract_source_suggest": {"input": "arXiv"}}], "primary_arxiv_category": ["quant-ph"], "external_system_identifiers": [{"schema": "ADS", "value": "2007EPJD...44..319S"}, {"schema": "SPIRES", "value": "SPIRES-6525350"}], "titles": [{"title": "A Bohmian view on quantum decoherence"}, {"source": "arXiv", "title": "A Bohmian view on quantum decoherence"}, {"source": "arXiv", "title": "A quantum trajectory description of decoherence"}], "facet_author_name": ["1975432_Florentino Borondo", "1972197_A.S. Sanz"], "_oai": {"sets": ["Literature"], "id": "oai:inspirehep.net:640163", "updated": "2026-02-06T10:00:14.491114"}, "curated": true, "journal_title_variants": ["Eur.Phys.J.D", "Eur. Phys. J. D"], "arxiv_eprints": [{"categories": ["quant-ph", "physics.chem-ph"], "value": "quant-ph/0310096"}]}, "links": {"bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/640163?format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/640163?format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/640163?format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/640163?format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/640163?format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/640163?format=cv", "citations": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A640163"}}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=arxiv%3Aquant-ph%2F0310096&size=5&page=1", "bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=arxiv%3Aquant-ph%2F0310096&size=5&page=1&format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=arxiv%3Aquant-ph%2F0310096&size=5&page=1&format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=arxiv%3Aquant-ph%2F0310096&size=5&page=1&format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=arxiv%3Aquant-ph%2F0310096&size=5&page=1&format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=arxiv%3Aquant-ph%2F0310096&size=5&page=1&format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=arxiv%3Aquant-ph%2F0310096&size=5&page=1&format=cv"}}